        "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "You are writing a YouTube video description for the channel \"CHANNEL_NAME\".\n\nThe channel is about: CHANNEL_TOPIC\n\nWrite the description for the video named at the bottom. Cover only what that filename actually names. If it names a specific tool, product, place, person or event, stay on that subject and do not broaden it out.\n\nHOW TO WRITE IT:\n- Open with two or three sentences telling the viewer what they get from watching. Vary this opening between videos. Never reuse the same formula twice.\n- Then write two or three short paragraphs, 2 to 4 sentences each. Work the natural search terms for this subject in, but write for a person, not a search engine.\n- Match the tone to the subject and to what this channel is about.\n- Plain sentences in the body. No emoji, no all-caps words, no headings or labels, and no decorative symbols anywhere except the separator line described below.\n- Never invent a fact, figure, date or year. If you are not certain of something, leave it out.\n- After the paragraphs, leave a blank line and then add these links, each on its own line, exactly as written and with nothing added:\n  LINK_1\n  LINK_2\n- Then a separator line, on its own line, exactly: ───────────────\n- Then a short disclaimer, 2 to 3 sentences. It must say that the views expressed are the creator's own opinion and that the video is for general information and entertainment, and that viewers should do their own research before acting on anything in it. If the subject is financial, medical, legal or otherwise regulated, add one line making clear this is not professional advice. Do not add that line for subjects where it would make no sense. Word it freshly, do not copy this instruction back verbatim.\n- Then the same separator line again, on its own line, exactly: ───────────────\n- Finish with 3 to 5 lowercase hashtags on a single line, relevant to the subject.\n\nOutput the finished description text and nothing else. No preamble, no explanation, no quote marks around it.\n\nThe video filename is: {{4.name}}",
            "inputType": "single"
          }
        ],
